      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285, we need to determine the greatest common divisor (GCD) of these two numbers. Let's start by finding the prime factorizations of 342 and 285.\n\nFirst, we factorize 342:\n\\[\n342 \\div 2 = 171\n\\]\n\\[\n171 \\div 3 = 57\n\\]\n\\[\n57 \\div 3 = 19\n\\]\n\\[\n19 \\div 19 = 1\n\\]\nSo, the prime factorization of 342 is:\n\\[\n342 = 2 \\times 3^2 \\times 19\n\\]\n\nNext, we factorize 285:\n\\[\n285 \\div 3 = 95\n\\]\n\\[\n95 \\div 5 = 19\n\\]\n\\[\n19 \\div 19 = 1\n\\]\nSo, the prime factorization of 285 is:\n\\[\n285 = 3 \\times 5 \\times 19\n\\]\n\nNow, we identify the common prime factors of 342 and 285. The common prime factors are 3 and 19. The lowest power of these common prime factors is \\(3^1\\) and \\(19^1\\). Therefore, the GCD of 342 and 285 is:\n\\[\n3^1 \\times 19^1 = 3 \\times 19 = 57\n\\]\n\nThus, the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285 is \\(\\boxed{57}\\).",
